      "side": 1,
      "message": "This issue is probably seen only with some custom downstream governors. In mainline we have a mechanism for schedutil governor to rebuild the sched domains. You can see it in the function:\nsched_cpufreq_governor_change(), which is called after register_em() from cpufreq_init_policy().\n\nIn that function sched_cpufreq_governor_change(), there is a check if governor is schedutil_gov only then rebuild the sched domains.\nLook at the comment there: \"EAS shouldn\u0027t be attempted without sugov...\"\n\nIMO we should change that function to always rebuild the shced domain when there is new policy, not only when schedutil gov is involved.",
      "revId": "436019789cf732fbf93d31b9b5c03967d78a9e6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
