      "message": "static int cpufreq_online(unsigned int cpu)\n\n  blocking_notifier_call_chain(\u0026cpufreq_policy_notifier_list,\n                               CPUFREQ_CREATE_POLICY, policy);\n\n  if (cpufreq_driver-\u003eregister_em)\n      cpufreq_driver-\u003eregister_em(policy);\n\nmainline code:\n\nxxx_cpufreq_register_em()\n\n  em_dev_register_perf_domain()\n\n    em_create_pd()                                                       \u003c--- (1)\n\n    dev_info(dev, \"EM: created perf domain\\n\")\n      \n\nstatic struct notifier_block init_cpu_capacity_notifier \u003d {\n        .notifier_call \u003d init_cpu_capacity_callback,\n};\n\nregister_cpufreq_notifier()\n\n  ret \u003d cpufreq_register_notifier(\u0026init_cpu_capacity_notifier,\n                                  CPUFREQ_POLICY_NOTIFIER);\n\ninit_cpu_capacity_callback()\n\n  schedule_work(\u0026update_topology_flags_work)\n\n    update_topology_flags_workfn()\n\n      rebuild_sched_domains()\n\n        partition_sched_domains()\n\n          partition_sched_domains_locked()\n\n            /* !!! this is called initially even w/!sched_energy_update\n             * because of the if condition w/ the cpumasks is failing */ \n            has_eas |\u003d build_perf_domains(doms_new[i]);                   \u003c--- (2)      \n\nSo on your platform (2) is called before (1)? Android code might be slightly different ...\n\nIs the relation to https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/bdfa61448f3184fb8a48f25da621532fcbef3d3a%5E%21 that w/o this patch\nyou would have rebuild the scheduler domain hierarchy with the change to schedutil_gov? Are you using this governor? Or is this unrelated?\n",
